    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-062. **Synthetic-fixture verified** — the Wikipedia gradient target is triple-blocked.\n\n## The verified delta (fixture, 2026-11-02)\n\n5-row fixture at `docs/adr062-gradient-test.html`:\n\n| Row | CSS | Render |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `background-color: #d35400` (control) | Solid orange ✓ |\n| 2 | `linear-gradient(red, blue)` (default 180deg) | **Vertical red→blue** ✓ |\n| 3 | `linear-gradient(45deg, red, blue)` | Diagonal ✓ |\n| 4 | `linear-gradient(to right, red, white, blue)` | Horizontal 3-stop ✓ |\n| 5 | `linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0), white)` | Gray→white ✓ |\n\n**All 5 render correctly.** First gradient rendered by HoneyBee.\n\n## The angle math correction\n\nFirst implementation used math convention (`cos θ, sin θ` for direction). Rendered **horizontal instead of vertical** for the default 180deg case — CSS linear-gradient angles are measured from \"up\" clockwise, in screen coordinates (y down).\n\n**Correct formula** (CSS Images 3 §3.1.1):\n- Direction: `(sin θ, -cos θ)` in screen coords\n- Length: `L = W·|sin θ| + H·|cos θ|`\n\n| CSS angle | Direction | Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0° | up | (0, -1) |\n| 90° | right | (1, 0) |\n| 180° | down (default) | (0, 1) |\n| 270° | left | (-1, 0) |\n\nPre-fix, all angles were rotated 90°. Post-fix, all map correctly.\n\n## The unplanned prerequisite\n\n**`parse_color` had no `rgb()` / `rgba()` support.** Wikipedia's gradient starts with `rgba(255,255,255,0)` — without rgba parsing, the first stop silently fails, leaving 1 stop, no gradient paint.\n\n**Extended `parse_color`** (~50 lines): `rgb(r, g, b)` / `rgba(r, g, b, a)` with integer (0-255), percentage (0-100%), and mixed channel forms.\n\n**Same pattern as ADR-060's `#include` discovery** — a prerequisite the spec assumed existed but didn't. Bundled into the same commit, recorded honestly.\n\n## The three pre-shipping bugs\n\n1. **`parse_color` had no rgb/rgba** — caught by pre-patch diagnostic\n2. **`split_tokens` not in `layout.cpp`'s scope** — caught by first build\n3. **Angle math 90° rotated** — caught by fixture screenshot\n\n**Same discipline as ADR-057/058/059/060**: each cycle's bugs caught at the earliest possible check (diagnostic → build → fixture), never after shipping.\n\n## What ships\n\n| Layer | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `parse_color` | `rgb()` / `rgba()` support (~50 lines) |\n| Parser | `linear-gradient(...)` preserved as `background-image: <raw>` |\n| LayoutBox | `background_is_gradient` + angle + stops vector |\n| Layout | `parse_background_gradient` helper (~60 lines) |\n| Paint | `paint_background_gradient` with CSS §3.1.1 formula |\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- **Zero Wikipedia delta.** Target is:\n  ```css\n  .vector-sticky-pinned-container::after {\n      background: linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0), white);\n      position: sticky;\n  }\n  ```\n  Triple-blocked: (1) `::after` pseudo-element, (2) `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` is `h=0` (ADR-050), (3) `position: sticky` deferred.\n\n- **No stop positions** — parsed but treated as uniform (`red 20%` interpolates at 1/(N-1) instead of 20%).\n- **No radial / conic / repeating.**\n- **No multi-layer.**\n\n## The grammar is now complete\n\n**11/11 `background:` forms parse.** 10/11 render on Wikipedia. The 11th (linear-gradient) parses + paints but is ancestor-culled.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 683 → 687 cases (+4 new)\n- 2614 → 2627 assertions (+13)\n- 1 test flipped (ADR-055's \"gradient dropped\" → \"preserved\")\n- Zero regression on 683 pre-existing tests\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Stop positions (uniform interpolation applied)\n- Radial / conic / repeating gradients\n- Multi-layer gradients\n- Color interpolation spaces (`in oklab`)\n- `position: sticky` (target's third blocker)\n- Ancestor culling unblock (target's second blocker)\n\nRefs #265\n",
